\section*{Appendix: Runtime Verification Protocol}

This appendix documents the runtime verification procedures applied to
the MK-15 suprakernel during multi-domain evolution. All verification
steps were executed in parallel with the suprakernel operator
$\mathcal{F}_{\text{SK}}$, ensuring continuous integrity monitoring,
constraint enforcement, and ledger-bound reproducibility.

\subsection*{A. Runtime State Capture}

At each iteration $n$, the suprakernel records the full state vector
\[
\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)} =
\begin{bmatrix}
\mathbf{X}_{\text{passive}}^{(n)} \\
\mathbf{X}_{\text{active}}^{(n)} \\
\mathbf{X}_{\text{semi}}^{(n)}
\end{bmatrix},
\]
along with all domain-specific constraint margins. The capture is
performed prior to perturbation damping to ensure accurate transient
logging.

\subsection*{B. Constraint Verification}

For each iteration, the constraint envelope
\[
\mathcal{C}_{\text{SK}} =
\mathcal{C}_{\text{passive}}
\wedge
\mathcal{C}_{\text{active}}
\wedge
\mathcal{C}_{\text{semi}}
\wedge
\mathcal{C}_{\text{thermal}}
\wedge
\mathcal{C}_{\text{ledger}}
\wedge
\mathcal{C}_{\text{enc}}
\]
is evaluated. The runtime enforces
\[
\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)} \in \mathcal{C}_{\text{SK}}
\quad
\forall n,
\]
with violations flagged for immediate damping or termination.

\subsection*{C. Perturbation Monitoring}

Perturbations are measured as
\[
\delta \mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)} =
\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)} -
\mathcal{F}_{\text{SK}}\big(\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n-1)}, \Delta t\big),
\]
and the damping operator verifies the contraction bound
\[
\|\delta \mathbf{X}'_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}\|
\le
\kappa \|\delta \mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}\|,
\quad 0 < \kappa < 1.
\]

\subsection*{D. Thermal Shock Gradient Logging}

Thermal shock gradients are computed as
\[
G_{\text{TS}}^{(n)} =
\delta_{1}\lambda_{\min}(\mathbf{K}_{\text{th}}^{(n)})
-
\delta_{2}\lambda_{\max}(\mathbf{C}_{\text{th}}^{(n)})
-
\delta_{3}\lambda_{\max}(\mathbf{S}_{\text{shock}}^{(n)}),
\]
with admissibility enforced by
\[
\text{SM}_{\text{TS}}^{(n)} =
G_{\text{TS}}^{(n)} - G_{\text{crit,TS}} \ge 0.
\]

\subsection*{E. Encrypted Runtime Binding}

Each iteration produces an encrypted runtime block
\[
\Lambda^{(n)} =
\mathcal{E}_{\text{SK}}\big(\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}, k_{\text{sec}}\big),
\]
which is bound to a ledger entry
\[
\ell^{(n)} =
\mathcal{L}_{\text{SK}}\big(\mathbf{X}_{\text{SK}}^{(n)}, \Lambda^{(n)}\big).
\]

\subsection*{F. Sovereign Ledger Verification}

The sovereign ledger chain is updated via
\[
H^{(n)} =
\text{Hash}\big(\ell^{(n)} \,\|\, H^{(n-1)}\big),
\]
ensuring immutability, collision resistance, and full traceability of
the suprakernel evolution sequence.

\subsection*{G. Verification Outcome}

All iterations satisfied the constraint envelope, perturbation
contraction bound, thermal shock margin, and ledger integrity
requirements. The runtime verification protocol confirms that the MK-15
suprakernel evolution is reproducible, stable, and cryptographically
sealed across the entire test sequence.